## 25. Ranking algorithm

Use the following ranking priority:

**Primary criterion:**
Higher total points rank first.

**Secondary criterion:**
If teams have equal points, the team with the lower total recorded response time ranks first.

**Third criterion:**
If points and total response time are identical, assign the same rank.

Example:

| Team | Points | Total response time | Rank |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Team A | 40 | 35 seconds | 1 |
| Team B | 40 | 48 seconds | 2 |
| Team C | 30 | 25 seconds | 3 |

This means Team A ranks above Team B because both have 40 points, but Team A has a lower total response time.

Make the ranking logic consistent on the backend.

Do not calculate different rankings separately in different frontend components.

